Keep vllm.parser.harmony importable without xgrammar >= 0.1.34.

harmony.py imports `xgrammar.openai_tool_call_schema` at module level. That
module first appears in xgrammar 0.1.34; nixpkgs ships 0.1.33, on master too.
vLLM asks for xgrammar >= 0.2.1, but pythonRelaxDeps drops the pin, so the
mismatch surfaces as a crash rather than at the dependency check:

    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'xgrammar.openai_tool_call_schema'

Guard the import here rather than at each importer. Four modules pull in
vllm.parser.harmony -- vllm/parser/__init__.py and
entrypoints/openai/responses/streaming_events.py eagerly, parser_manager and
responses/context.py lazily -- so guarding any one of them just moves the
crash to the next. BuiltinToolParam and FunctionToolParam are used only as
annotations (harmony.py:451-452), so Any is a faithful stand-in.

Everything else harmony.py needs from xgrammar exists in 0.1.33: StructuralTag
and all eleven names it imports from xgrammar.structural_tag.

Bumping xgrammar instead is a worse trade: 0.2.x swaps nanobind for
apache-tvm-ffi in its build-system, obsoleting the nanobind patch nixpkgs
carries, and 0.2.5 pins transformers <5 while vLLM 0.28.0 needs >= 5.5.3.
Only 0.2.6rc2 lifts that bound.

--- a/vllm/parser/harmony.py
+++ b/vllm/parser/harmony.py
@@ -11,7 +11,17 @@
 
 from openai_harmony import HarmonyError, Message, Role
 from xgrammar import StructuralTag
-from xgrammar.openai_tool_call_schema import BuiltinToolParam, FunctionToolParam
+
+try:
+    from xgrammar.openai_tool_call_schema import BuiltinToolParam, FunctionToolParam
+except ModuleNotFoundError:
+    # xgrammar < 0.1.34 has no openai_tool_call_schema. Both names are used
+    # only as annotations below, so Any keeps the module importable.
+    from typing import Any
+
+    BuiltinToolParam = Any
+    FunctionToolParam = Any
+
 from xgrammar.structural_tag import (
     AnyTextFormat,
     ConstStringFormat,
